<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Tondo</h1><p class="st-meta">900 CE – 1589 CE (approx.) · capital Tondo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Tagalog trading polity on Manila Bay, named in the Laguna Copperplate Inscription of 900 and ruled by Lakandula when the Spanish arrived.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laguna-copperplate-inscription">Laguna Copperplate Inscription</a>, dated 900 and the oldest known document from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/philippines">Philippines</a>, mentions a leader of Tundun, generally identified with Tondo. The settlement grew on the northern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasig-river">Pasig River</a> delta, trading with Chinese merchants, who knew the region as Lusong.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Tondo was ruled by a lakan or paramount chief over a society of maginoo nobles, maharlika warriors and dependants. It traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and gold for Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and had close ties with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/brunei-sultanate">Brunei</a>. By the 16th century parts of the elite had adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, while most people kept indigenous beliefs.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-lopez-de-legazpi">Miguel Lopez de Legazpi</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-maynila">Maynila</a> in 1571, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakandula">Lakandula</a> accepted Spanish rule and was baptised. In 1587 to 1588 his relatives led the Tondo conspiracy to expel the Spanish, which was discovered and its leaders executed or exiled. Tondo became a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/captaincy-general-of-the-philippines">Captaincy General of the Philippines</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-tondo.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Tondo" width="320" height="349"><figcaption>Image: Delirium333 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Tondo_(1570).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 CE – 1589 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tondo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lakandula, Agustin de Legazpi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tagalog indigenous religion, Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Tagalog</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/philippines">Philippines</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tondo, Tundun, Lusong</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1244&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tondo" aria-label="Kingdom of Tondo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7988 1634 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Tondo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8308 1890L8178 2269M8308 1890L8309 1890"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8178 2269h0M8309 1890h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8308 1890h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8308 1890h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tondo. <a href="/atlas?year=1244&amp;focus=kingdom-of-tondo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

